---
import LegalLayout from "@/layouts/LegalLayout.astro";

const updated = "June 1, 2026";
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Terms of Service"
  eyebrow="Terms"
  updated={updated}
  description="These terms describe the rules for using Callisto, a macOS menu bar app for viewing and managing meeting-related Google Calendar events."
>
  <h2>Agreement</h2>
  <p>
    By downloading, installing, or using Callisto, you agree to these Terms of
    Service. If you do not agree, do not use the app.
  </p>

  <h2>The Service</h2>
  <p>
    Callisto is a menu bar only macOS application for viewing and managing
    meetings stored in Google Calendar. The app can show upcoming events, open
    meeting links, sync selected calendars, and perform event actions you
    choose, such as RSVP updates or deleting/removing events when your Google
    account permissions allow it.
  </p>

  <h2>Google Account Access</h2>
  <p>
    Some Callisto features require you to connect a Google account and grant
    Google Calendar permissions. You are responsible for the Google account you
    connect, the calendars you access, and the event actions you perform through
    Callisto. Google services remain governed by Google's own terms and
    policies.
  </p>

  <h2>Your Responsibilities</h2>
  <p>You agree not to use Callisto to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Access calendars or events that you are not authorized to access.</li>
    <li>
      Interfere with Google Calendar, GitHub, Cloudflare, or any related
      service.
    </li>
    <li>
      Violate applicable law, third-party rights, or workplace policies that
      apply to your calendar data.
    </li>
    <li>
      Reverse engineer, redistribute, or modify Callisto except where allowed by
      applicable law or an applicable open-source license.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Local Data and Privacy</h2>
  <p>
    Callisto stores OAuth tokens in the macOS Keychain and stores app data
    locally on your Mac. The
    <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a>
    explains what data Callisto accesses, how that data is used, and how to remove
    local account access.
  </p>

  <h2>Updates and Downloads</h2>
  <p>
    Callisto may check for app updates using Sparkle and GitHub release
    metadata. Downloading or updating the app may involve GitHub and normal
    network connection data handled by GitHub or your network provider.
  </p>

  <h2>Availability and Changes</h2>
  <p>
    Callisto is provided as an evolving app. Features may change, break, be
    removed, or depend on third-party services that change independently,
    including Google Calendar APIs, GitHub releases, Cloudflare hosting, and
    macOS platform behavior.
  </p>

  <h2>No Warranty</h2>
  <p>
    Callisto is provided "as is" and "as available" without warranties of any
    kind, to the maximum extent permitted by law. The app may contain bugs or
    display incomplete, delayed, or incorrect calendar information. Always
    verify important meeting details in Google Calendar or the original meeting
    source.
  </p>

  <h2>Limitation of Liability</h2>
  <p>
    To the maximum extent permitted by law, the Callisto maintainers will not be
    liable for indirect, incidental, consequential, special, exemplary, or
    punitive damages, or for lost profits, lost data, missed meetings, business
    interruption, or calendar changes made through your account.
  </p>

  <h2>Termination</h2>
  <p>
    You may stop using Callisto at any time. You may remove connected Google
    accounts in the app and revoke Callisto's access from your Google Account.
    Access to Callisto may be changed or discontinued at any time.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to These Terms</h2>
  <p>
    These terms may be updated as Callisto changes. Continued use of Callisto
    after an updated version is published means you accept the updated terms.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    For questions about these terms, contact the Callisto maintainers through
    <a href="https://github.com/2fd/callisto/issues">GitHub Issues</a>.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
